  "title": "Riccio-2024-training-10.3390/data9050061",
  "description": "This derivative dataset redistributes 20 per-patient feature tables computed from the Freiburg intracranial EEG database for epilepsy analysis. Each row is a 2-second sliding window (1-second step) with 1080 univariate and bivariate features extracted from six electrodes across six frequency bands, labelled by seizure phase (pre-ictal, ictal, post-ictal, inter-ictal). The tables are intended as training data for machine-learning seizure detection and are byte-identical to the original Zenodo release. No raw recordings are included.",
  "methods_description": "Six intracranial EEG electrodes per patient (three in the epileptic focus, three outside it) were band-pass filtered into six bands (alpha, beta1, beta2, low, medium and high gamma). Features were computed with the Training Builder tool in 2-s windows with a 1-s step from 256 Hz recordings. Each window has 14 univariate and 8 bivariate features per electrode and band, giving 1080 features, and was labelled by seizure phase.",
